      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">a 0.4 mm single-layer sheet</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was molded under the same conditions as those for the A layer by using the resin composition of B layer having 70 parts by weight of polyethylene having the melting point of 135° C., viscosity-average molecular weight of 700,000, and molecular weight distribution of 6.0, 20 parts by weight of polyethylene having the melting point of 135° C., viscosity-average molecular weight of 250,000, and molecular weight distribution of 6.0, and 10 parts by weight of homopolymer polypropylene having the melting point of 160° C., viscosity-average molecular weight of 400,000, and molecular weight distribution of 10.0.</span>
